{"conclusion":"A replaying counter signed by an unbound key is refused before replay and leaves its claim BACKED; #170 still requires a binding in .warrant/trust.json.","duty":"57cf328ea7612260feabafbf401915e4325e1f8e2c68c090fec7595f7b458acc","item":0,"kind":"obligation-closure-verdict-evidence","limits":["Only this obligation and its counter admission path were reviewed.","No production source, policy, bindings or test files are changed by this verdict.","The counter and challenge used in the reproduction are confined to disposable fixtures; the committed blob contains the complete script and observations.","The signed challenge records whose ids appear in the observations are fixture records, not records filed in the canonical store."],"observed":[{"baseline_check":[],"bound_control":{"check":[],"kind":"LOWERS","standing":"COUNTERED"},"challenge":"1ef9011daa60d31fdb2ccdcc137c66afb8a77c25d127e809f6c2344042867638","claim":"SPEC-3.2-20","counter_blob":"8a29a3c194f8211559a77b55b88a2c23171de30f80faf936306b51cdc63664fe","counter_replay":null,"revision":"3f2be6aa03e584923caae9bd60a38f3687bf2dd7","unbound":{"check":[["UNAUTHENTIC","records/1ef9011daa60d31fdb2ccdcc137c66afb8a77c25d127e809f6c2344042867638.json: signed by a key the trust does not bind"]],"cli_error":"REFUSED key 99a90050fc17 is not bound to 'g1-unbound-counter-probe' in .warrant/trust.json","cli_exit":2,"in_challenge_table":false,"model_bad":"signed by a key the trust does not bind","standing":"BACKED"}},{"baseline_check":[],"bound_control":{"check":[],"kind":"LOWERS","standing":"COUNTERED"},"challenge":"e40fc355a527fb348af6d8a1b437d151e7e48afcbe86b8ed4abd2aa94586e863","claim":"SPEC-3.2-20","counter_blob":"4cdb38d07d90c57d370ba8fad336ff3591f68eb22fc3c1328400cd469b88f2d9","counter_replay":null,"revision":"f79c1b58d8f3ad872ac0f4aaa6889a108ba8953a","unbound":{"check":[["UNAUTHENTIC","records/e40fc355a527fb348af6d8a1b437d151e7e48afcbe86b8ed4abd2aa94586e863.json: signed by a key the trust does not bind"]],"cli_error":"REFUSED key ba0f82773ec6 is not bound to 'g1-unbound-counter-probe' in .warrant/trust.json","cli_exit":2,"in_challenge_table":false,"model_bad":"signed by a key the trust does not bind","standing":"BACKED"}}],"owed":"A counter blob (warrant-claims/counter@1) that replays in check is accepted whoever signed it, with no key bound in .warrant/trust.json.","reason":"T establishes self-certifying bindings without an administrator. D expressly owes acceptance without a key bound in the repository trust file. Those differ: all of #170's stranger fixtures bind a key, including claims selftest challenge_by and circle_test.Fix. The unbound path is still refused. This is an unmet obligation, not an assertion that removing general record authentication is the correct implementation.","refs":["s0fractal/warrant#170","merge 3f2be6aa03e584923caae9bd60a38f3687bf2dd7"],"reproduction":{"instructions":["Make a disposable clean checkout of each reviewed revision, install its runtime dependencies, and set TMPDIR to a writable directory under ~/.warrant.","Save script as probe.py outside that checkout and run python3 probe.py <disposable-checkout>. It modifies only that fixture and creates then deletes a fresh fixture signing seed outside the checkout.","The probe first requires check(base=HEAD) == [], builds a real M234 counter against SPEC-3.2-20, and requires replay_counter == None.","It tests both the CLI refusal and a correctly signed directly filed challenge with no binding, then adds only that key's self-certifying binding as a positive control. The same signed record and counter must then yield LOWERS, COUNTERED, and a clean check(base=HEAD)."],"script":"\"\"\"Reproduce the G1 unbound-counter gap using a real M234 counter replay.\n\nRun in a disposable checkout at the revision being assessed. Never reads any\noperator key. The fresh key is used only to sign this fixture's counter.\n\"\"\"\nimport importlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nroot = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\nsys.path.insert(0, str(root))\nsys.path.insert(0, str(root / \"tools\"))\nos.environ.pop(\"WARRANT_CLAIMS_TRUST\", None)\nCL = importlib.import_module(\"claims\")\nfrom warrant import Key, records as R\nfrom warrant import jcs as C\nfrom warrant.store import Store\n\ntry:\n    patch_for = CL._mutant_patch\nexcept AttributeError:\n    from claimslib.audit import _mutant_patch as patch_for\n\nrev = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], cwd=root, text=True).strip()\nrepo = CL.Repo(root)\nbaseline = CL.check(repo, base=rev)\nassert baseline == [], baseline\nmodel = CL.Model(repo.snapshot(), repo.trust())\nn = model.current[\"SPEC-3.2-20\"]\nrepo.mutants()\ndoc = {\n    \"counter\": CL.COUNTER,\n    \"claim\": n.id,\n    \"against\": n.tid,\n    \"patch\": patch_for(repo, \"M234\"),\n    \"passes\": sorted(n.doc[\"witnesses\"]),\n    \"fails\": [\"records_test:I5\"],\n    \"why\": \"M234 changes a statement covered by M232 while the claim's cited witnesses pass.\",\n}\nassert doc[\"patch\"]\nstore = Store(repo.store_dir)\nh = store.put_json(doc)\nreplay = CL.replay_counter(repo, repo.snapshot(), h, n)\nassert replay is None, replay\nactor = \"g1-unbound-counter-probe\"\nkey = Key.generate()\nseed = root.parent / (root.name + \".probe.seed\")\nseed.write_text(key.seed_hex() + \"\\n\")\ncounter_file = root.parent / (root.name + \".counter.json\")\ncounter_file.write_text(json.dumps(doc))\nrun = subprocess.run([\n    sys.executable, str(root / \"tools\" / \"claims.py\"), \"--root\", str(root),\n    \"challenge\", \"--key\", str(seed), \"--actor\", actor, \"--claim\", n.id,\n    \"--because\", \"G1 unbound counter probe\", \"--counter-file\", str(counter_file),\n], cwd=root, capture_output=True, text=True)\nseed.unlink()\nassert run.returncode == 2 and \"not bound\" in run.stderr, run\nrid = store.put_record(R.record(\"challenge\", actor, 1793000000,\n    R.challenge(n.tid, \"G1 unbound counter probe\", [h], 0)), key)\nunbound_model = CL.Model(repo.snapshot(), repo.trust())\nunbound_table = CL.challenge_table(repo, unbound_model)\nCL.cmd_project(repo)\nunbound_check = CL.check(repo, base=rev)\nassert rid in unbound_model.bad and rid not in unbound_table\nassert CL.status_of(unbound_model.current[n.id], CL.lowered(unbound_table)) == \"BACKED\"\nassert any(c == \"UNAUTHENTIC\" and rid[:12] in why for c, why in unbound_check), unbound_check\nunbound_result = {\n    \"cli_exit\": run.returncode,\n    \"cli_error\": run.stderr.strip(),\n    \"model_bad\": unbound_model.bad[rid],\n    \"in_challenge_table\": rid in unbound_table,\n    \"standing\": \"BACKED\",\n    \"check\": unbound_check,\n}\n# Only the signed self-certifying binding changes: same key, record, blob,\n# claim, source and real replay. This is the positive control.\ntrust_path = root / \".warrant\" / \"trust.json\"\nbindings = C.loads(trust_path.read_bytes())\nbindings[\"keys\"].append({\"actor\": actor, \"public\": key.public,\n                         \"proof\": CL.binding_proof(key, actor)})\ntrust_path.write_bytes(C.canon(bindings))\nbound_model = CL.Model(repo.snapshot(), repo.trust())\nbound_table = CL.challenge_table(repo, bound_model)\nCL.cmd_project(repo)\nbound_check = CL.check(repo, base=rev)\nassert bound_table[rid][\"kind\"] == \"LOWERS\", bound_table.get(rid)\nassert CL.status_of(bound_model.current[n.id], CL.lowered(bound_table)) == \"COUNTERED\"\nassert bound_check == [], bound_check\nprint(json.dumps({\n    \"revision\": rev,\n    \"baseline_check\": baseline,\n    \"counter_replay\": replay,\n    \"claim\": n.id,\n    \"counter_blob\": h,\n    \"challenge\": rid,\n    \"unbound\": unbound_result,\n    \"bound_control\": {\"kind\": bound_table[rid][\"kind\"], \"standing\": \"COUNTERED\", \"check\": bound_check},\n}, indent=2))\n"},"reviewed_master":"f79c1b58d8f3ad872ac0f4aaa6889a108ba8953a","reviewed_subject":"3f2be6aa03e584923caae9bd60a38f3687bf2dd7","transition":"fbcccb2989a75d24f9030